\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {\mbox  {VII-A}}Gauge pinning (Cor.\nobreakspace  {}5.2 in closed loop)}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Three phases of the GNSS-denied transit (supplementary video S2). Left: gauge free --- the five ghost caissons (each agent's own load estimate) drift \emph  {coherently}, overlapping each other while offset from truth. Middle: the beacon pins one agent; the fleet is mid-convergence. Right: converged through the turn. Single illustrative run, median-$D_{ss}$ seed by the documented selection rule.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:montage}{{1}{5}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Error-transport holonomy amplitude on both plants. Thm\nobreakspace  {}7.2 (leading-order, deterministic): Tier-1 slope 1.999 with switch-offs at machine zero; Drake slope 2.000 with the $m{=}2$ coefficient check at 1.0000, the $\eta {=}0$ switch-off at machine zero, and the parallel class suppressing the coefficient $31\times $ (achieved-$\varepsilon $; exact cancellation remains the Tier-1 machine-zero result).}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:f4a}{{2}{5}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {\mbox  {VII-B}}The theorem's object, measured on both plants}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {\mbox  {VII-C}}The closed-loop floor: the conjecture falsified, coherently}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {\mbox  {VII-D}}Variance attribution: what makes up disagreement}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {\mbox  {VII-E}}Symmetry: protection lives on the amplitude object}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {\mbox  {VII-F}}Cross-tier coefficients and the validity domain}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Tier-1/Tier-2 agreement on the conjectured steady-state floor ([ES\nobreakspace  {}\S  10(ii)]). Panel\nobreakspace  {}(a) separately tests the leading-order, deterministic holonomy amplitude of Thm\nobreakspace  {}7.2 in both tiers. With $D_0$ measured in situ by straight-tow controls, the fitted excess exponents are 1.101 [1.076, 1.125] (Tier-1) and 1.077 [1.054, 1.102] (Drake); the pre-registered equivalence test passes ($+0.023$ [$-0.012$, $+0.057$] $\subset $ [$-0.2$, $0.2$]) and the conjectured order\nobreakspace  {}2 is excluded on both plants. The fitted slope is a measured quantity in the conjectured regime, carried with the mixture caveat; the CIs exclude order\nobreakspace  {}1 as well, and no first-order law is asserted.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:f4b}{{3}{5}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces All Drake arms on matched formation draws. Ablating the conjugated transport (A2) runs $1.7\times \!\to \!8.2\times $ above the paper rule with growing $\tau $; naive consensus (A1) holds disagreement flat and low---by groupthink (anchored ANEES 62, drift 8.4\nobreakspace  {}m): agreement alone is never a virtue metric. The straight-tow control shows the motion excitation ($19$--$21\times $ at every $\tau $).}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:f4c}{{4}{5}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {\mbox  {VII-G}}Numerics defense}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Two objects, two panels, never mixed. (a)\nobreakspace  {}The amplitude departure from the symmetric class is first-order in $\varepsilon $ (measured 1.006, base commutator exactly zero). (b)\nobreakspace  {}The closed-loop floor excess: the seed-paired estimator gives slope 1.58 [1.44, 1.84] at every $\tau $ --- excluding both the conjectured 2 and 1; segment slopes rise 1.2\,$\to $\,2.1 up the ladder, consistent with a linear-plus-quadratic mixture that the registered single-power model mis-specifies.}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:f5}{{5}{6}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Connectivity buys agreement, not anchoring. The pre-anchor floor improves with $\lambda _2$ (a); single-anchor pinning is anchor-rate-limited (b, Spearman $+0.04$); re-agreement around the pin \emph  {anti}-orders with connectivity (c, $-0.51\,[-0.65, -0.36]$). With the in-domain contraction claim verified (Fig.\nobreakspace  {}7\hbox {}), this is the pre-registered ES-01 finding path, reported as such.}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:d9}{{6}{6}}
